Usage of inspect-deliveries-mysql:
  -address string
    	MySQL host:port
  -before-created-at string
    	exclusive cursor time in RFC3339 with microsecond precision
  -before-id string
    	exclusive page cursor UUID; requires before-created-at
  -ca string
    	optional PEM CA file; defaults to system trust
  -database string
    	shared logical application database
  -delivery string
    	optional delivery UUID for one detail record
  -isolated-fixture
    	plaintext only for explicitly enabled mysql:3306 disposable fixture
  -limit int
    	page size 1..1000, across all tenant queues (default 100)
  -password-env string
    	password environment variable (default "DATA_MODEL_MYSQL_INSPECTION_PASSWORD")
  -server-name string
    	TLS server name; defaults to address hostname
  -tenant string
    	explicit authorized tenant UUID
  -timeout duration
    	overall inspection deadline (default 30s)
  -user string
    	authorized read-only inspection account
